WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.660
______________________________________________________________
This has been one of my favorite anime of

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.660
this year.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.410
And as someone who gets off talking about
deep characters and complex story telling

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.830
for a living, I have to admit I'm a bit ashamed
of that.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:25.000
That time I got reincarnated as a slime has
so many things that should irritate me, starting

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.500
with that stupid - fitting title.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.870
The main character effortlessly gets more
and more powers, with practically no stakes.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.840
There is a sea of side characters introduced,
that I can't and won't all care about, and

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.780
there is no clear overarching narrative that
seems to tie the story together.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.210
Being a gourmet to the exquisite writing in
stories like One Piece, Jujutsu Kaisen or

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:54.840
Hunter x Hunter, I feel like I should be loathing
this piece of feel-good, escapist Isekai.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.760
And yet I god damn love it.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:09.430
I loved the first season and what's even worse,
I loved the second one even more.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:15.740
So whether you love or hate him, let me tell
you why I think that Rimuru Tempest is such

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.623
a fantastic character and why the blue slime
makes for such a refreshing story for me.

