00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.650
Link is in the description below, so once
we have discussed the story so far, make sure

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:14.820
to check it out!

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.220
There are two main things that make this anime
so great to me.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:25.130
The set-up of the story overall as well as
its main character Rimuru Tempest.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:35.840
The 

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:41.130
big strength of this story, is that it doesn't
try to be clever or pretends to be something

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.130
it is not.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:47.430
It doesn't try to preach any deep messages,
nor does it forcefully avert expectations

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:53.680
and tropes for the sake of it.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.930
It doesn't go out of its way to be creative,
but simply follows the rules of good writing.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.430
Characters are developed, the world is built
and everything that happens gets clean set-up

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:11.150
and foreshadowing.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:21.490
It 
doesn't try to break the rules, but follows

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.840
them with a lot of discipline.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:28.010
In other words, the anime knows what it is
and what it is not.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:33.010
And absurdly enough, I think that it's exactly
this authenticity alone that makes it already

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.120
stand out.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.740
The premise is as simple as the title suggests.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:42.990
A young man dies in our normal world and is
reborn as a slime in another world, only of

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:54.340
course that he gets ridiculous powers right
from the get-go.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.700
Classic Isekai escapism.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.459
From there on out, we basically follow our
slime hero, who shares our modern 21st century

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:07.030
perspective, as he discovers this new world,
gets stronger and stronger and starts building

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.540
a small nation.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:13.220
Like, maybe it's just me, but that premise
kind of hits a nerve with me.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:18.650
I've always loved strategic development games,
like Age of Empires, harvest moon or hell

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.030
even Minecraft.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:25.319
Yes, getting strong is part of the fun, but
the real struggle is in building something

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:26.319
big.

00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:30.720
So, as a kid, or even today sometimes, I like
to daydream about how it would be like to

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.130
be put into one of my favorite stories with
the best set of powers and how you could build

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.820
your own small comfortable place with it.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.820
Does that make any sense?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:45.250
And I think Fuse, the author of slime, I'm
just gonna call it slime from now on, it's

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:55.660
exactly what Fuse did when he created this
story.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.440
Rimuru is not a shouen hero, who has to get
stronger, or even a hero like Saitama, who

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.170
needs to grow on the inside.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:08.890
Rimuru already was a pretty decent leader
even as a human.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:14.040
His junior seems to like and respect him,
and while his character does have a dark side

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:24.460
to it sometimes, I think it's nothing that
has to be changed.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:29.380
Rimuru's character arc is not about growing
from a boy into a man or from a man into a

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:30.380
leader.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:35.960
It's about growing from a leader into a visionary,
that can change or form a whole society.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:42.540
So it's not about him getting stronger or
dealing with his emotions that we see, to

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:48.010
me it's about Rimuru growing to be the leader
not of a small team in his company, but that

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.910
of a whole nation.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:55.090
Learning about diplomacy and infrastructure
and the politics of the world, with the necessary

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.700
power to back it up.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:09.669
[Gazel saying that Rimuru is still naive]
That's what the story is about and why it's

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.169
so much fun.

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:14.919
It doesn't pretend to be anything more than
that.

00:06:14.919 --> 00:06:20.419
A major factor in this context, at least to
me, is the fact that Rimuru is a grown man,

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:23.350
that also acts like a grown man.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:30.020
He's a bit naive, but a quick learner and
most importantly, he is emotionally mature,

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.400
something that is so incredibly refreshing
for a main character.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:40.560
And it gives the entire story a certain maturity
as well when it comes to his actions, decisions

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:52.100
and relationships with other characters.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:57.750
Even the fan-service in the story, while undoubtedly
there, whole cow Shion can you walk with these,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.040
it's not as over the top as I feared at the
beginning.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:07.620
Plus it's surprisingly balanced between male
and female characters.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:13.140
The main themes that were easy to pick out
for me include racial equality, helping others,

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:18.210
leading others, individual growth, positive
civilization growth, choosing one’s battles,

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:21.660
and being compassionate yet rational.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:25.389
Those are all incredibly feel-good themes.

00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:31.139
But even though I usually prefer darker stories,
it works for me, because the Anime compromises

00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:37.199
this with some quite graphic imaging, but
more importantly a shift in focus between

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:38.199
the seasons.

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:53.320
Season 1 and 2 of slime felt very very coherent
when I first watched them, but now that the

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:59.979
season is over, I am shocked to say that this
is one of the rare cases where a season two

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:04.400
made the season one better.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.830
Season 1 is all about getting familiar with
our main character, a ton of world-building

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:12.610
and the establishment of the nation in Yura
forest.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:18.270
While this is a lot of fun to watch, to me
there were some big problems, should the story

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.100
have simply continued on like this.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.800
In season one there are are no stakes for
Rimuru and no personal challenges.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:32.120
Also, the focus on our slime made it absolutely
impossible to care for most, if any other

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:36.099
of the many characters thrown in with every
single season.

00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:40.300
At the end, the village is mostly a faceless
blob.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:45.660
Season 2 however, right off the bat I feel
did a fantastic job addressing all these potential

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:56.050
pitfalls.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:00.689
Rimuru loosing loosing Shion and many other
of his friends, not only gives him his first

00:09:00.689 --> 00:09:06.019
taste of reality and hardship, but also provides
some series development for his character,

00:09:06.019 --> 00:09:08.709
that pushes the narrative forward.

00:09:08.709 --> 00:09:13.569
He now has to deal with the fact, that the
3 rules he came up with on the fly in season

00:09:13.569 --> 00:09:19.269
one, were hasty and unsustainable in the face
of all the ill intent coming toward his new

00:09:19.269 --> 00:09:30.300
nation.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.439
Overall the story and world of slime takes
on a darker shade, which immediately satisfied

00:09:35.439 --> 00:09:38.430
people like me, who like some more complexity.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:43.559
Bust because Rimuru is strong doesn't mean
he can protect everyone all the time, and

00:09:43.559 --> 00:09:49.029
he starts handing off responsibility to more
and more of his followers.

00:09:49.029 --> 00:09:52.449
This solves the other big issue with season
one.

00:09:52.449 --> 00:09:57.809
Instead of endlessly adding more no-name characters
to the village, we get characterization for

00:09:57.809 --> 00:10:03.569
all those form season one, which left me which
a much better connection to characters like

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:07.209
Benimaru, Gobta and Shion than in the first
season.

00:10:07.209 --> 00:10:12.540
These characters now are not only powerful
themselves, but also act independently from

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.759
Rimuru.

00:10:14.759 --> 00:10:20.029
And all the characters that DO get added,
all have fantastic or at least interesting

00:10:20.029 --> 00:10:21.029
perosnalites.

00:10:21.029 --> 00:10:27.649
Ramiris, Diabolo and my boy Veldra all are
very easy to relate to, even though we got

00:10:27.649 --> 00:10:29.379
very little of them in season 1.

00:10:29.379 --> 00:10:38.490
And by the way I cant believe they had Veldra
do a Kamehameha.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:50.140
So, despite a very simple and text-book setup,
the story executes the rules of good storytelling

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:56.999
so well, that it's impossible for me not to
like it and be excited to see what comes next

00:10:56.999 --> 00:10:58.619
for Rimuru and co.

00:10:58.619 --> 00:11:02.819
I hope you want to watch a bit more, so check
out this video here next.

00:11:02.819 --> 00:11:06.449
Thanks for watching.

